          "message": "canonical NIST Fe II log-cosine repo layout (preserves all legacy outputs)\n\n- data/, scripts/, outputs/, tables/, tests/ canonical layout\n- scripts/nist_wct_log_spectral_scan_FIXED.py: prefer DataFrame.map over\n  applymap (silences pandas 2.1+ FutureWarning), behavior unchanged\n- scripts/run_feii_bin_stability.py: drives bins 120/160/200 for Fe II,\n  reuses existing canonical outputs unless --force, writes\n  tables/nist_master_results.csv\n- scripts/make_verdict.py: PASS/FAIL gate over the master CSV, writes\n  tables/nist_verdict.csv and updates the marker-delimited block in\n  RESULTS.md\n- scripts/nist_batch_run_neighbors.py: defaults retargeted to data/ and\n  outputs/batch_neighbors/\n- canonical outputs/fe_ion2_{120,160,200}/ populated from the existing\n  5000-null CuPy runs (sourced from outputs_fe_ion2_*_cupy_full/, which\n  remain untouched at repo root for provenance)\n- tests/test_nist_scanner.py: scanner --help, NIST cell cleaning,\n  wn(cm-1) detection, ion filter, master CSV schema, verdict requires\n  all three bins, k-stability tolerance, preservation guard (no\n  shutil.rmtree or rm -rf in scripts)\n- README.md rewritten around the log-spectral claim; no NIST-endorsement\n  language\n- RESULTS.md rewritten as concise machine-auditable summary; raw run log\n  preserved as RESULTS_legacy_log.md\n- requirements.txt added; .gitignore for __pycache__/.pytest_cache\n\nAll 20 historical outputs_* directories and the four root-level legacy\nscripts/CSVs are preserved untouched. Fe II verdict: PASS."
